{"version": "2026-08-30.2", "notes": ["Editable without code changes. Every slug must exist in profiles.vocabulary.TRADE_SLUGS.", "Matching is accent-folded and word-boundary anchored; multi-word entries match as phrases.", "priority orders which matched rule becomes primary (lower number wins).", "non_construction is evaluated ONLY when no trade rule fires, and never for rows", "whose category marks them as construction (see construction_markers).", "slug_sources records where each slug matched (title/category_raw/description); title-evidenced slugs are ordered first and become primary.", "A keyword must denote WORK PERFORMED, never only WHERE it happens. A bare location or surface noun matches every notice that mentions an address and classifies the trade by geography. 'chemin' did this: 'Deneigement des chemins municipaux' is snow clearing, and calling it roadwork was false regardless of what any downstream gate then did with it. Location nouns belong here only in phrase form, bound to a work word - 'refection de chemin', not 'chemin'. 'parc' did it worse: it fires on municipality names (Saint-Mathieu-du-Parc) and on the French sense of parc meaning a fleet or estate (parc de vehicules, parc immobilier), so the match itself is spurious rather than merely imprecise. tests/test_trade_location_nouns.py enforces this for the known cases."], "families": {"civil": ["roadwork", "sitework", "granular_supply", "bridge_structural", "concrete_flatwork", "water_wastewater", "utilities_underground", "marine_shoreline", "fencing_guiderail", "environmental_remediation"], "building": ["building_general", "building_envelope", "electrical", "mechanical_hvac", "demolition_abatement", "facility_maintenance"], "grounds": ["landscaping", "snow_ice_management"], "support": ["engineering_survey", "equipment_rental"]}, "construction_markers": {"category_normalized": ["construction"], "category_raw_keywords": ["cnst", "travaux de construction", "construction"]}, "rules": [{"slug": "bridge